---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import Terminal from "../../components/Terminal.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import {
  CLI_COMMANDS,
  RECORD_OUTPUT_HTML,
  REPLAY_OUTPUT_HTML,
  TEST_OUTPUT_HTML,
  INIT_HTML,
  FILE_STRUCTURE,
  REPRO_MD_CONTENT,
  ASSERTION_TYPES,
  SAVE_EXAMPLE,
  CI_WORKFLOW,
} from "../../content/snippets";
---

<Base title="Documentation — repro.md" description="Getting started with repro.md — installation, recording, replay, and CI setup.">

  <section style="padding-top: var(--space-2xl);">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <p class="section-label">Documentation</p>
      <h1 style="font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.25rem);">Getting started</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">Install repro, record a failure, replay it, and add it to CI.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Install -->
  <section>
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <h2 id="install">Install</h2>
      <CodeBlock filename="shell" id="install-cmd" code="npm install -g repro-md" />
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Or use <code>npx repro-md</code> without installing globally. Requires Node.js 20+.</p>
        <p>The agent you want to record (e.g. <code>claude</code>) must be installed separately &mdash; repro spawns it as a child process.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Init -->
  <section>
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <h2 id="init">Initialize</h2>
      <Terminal html={INIT_HTML} label="Initialize repro in your project" />
      <div class="prose">
        <p>This creates the <code>.repro/</code> directory for recordings and a <code>REPRO.md</code> manifest file.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Record -->
  <section>
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <h2 id="record">Record</h2>
      <Terminal html={RECORD_OUTPUT_HTML} label="Recording an agent run" />
      <div class="prose">
        <p>The proxy intercepts every model API call, forwards it to the real API, and records both the request and response. Secrets are redacted at capture time before anything touches disk.</p>
        <p>Recording requires a real <code>ANTHROPIC_API_KEY</code> &mdash; it makes real API calls. The proxy sets <code>ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL</code> to point the agent at the local proxy. The agent talks to the proxy thinking it's the real API.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Replay -->
  <section>
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <h2 id="replay">Replay</h2>
      <Terminal html={REPLAY_OUTPUT_HTML} label="Replaying a recorded run" />
      <div class="prose">
        <p>The agent runs in an isolated git worktree. Model responses come from the recorded trace. No API key required. No inference cost.</p>
        <p>Requests are matched by normalized SHA-256 hash of the message content, not by sequence number. In strict mode, a hash miss aborts and reports which message diverged. In lenient mode, it falls back to positional matching with warnings.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Test -->
  <section>
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <h2 id="test">Test</h2>
      <Terminal html={TEST_OUTPUT_HTML} label="Running all recorded failures as regression tests" />
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Replays all open failures listed in <code>REPRO.md</code>. Exit code 0 if all pass, 1 otherwise.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Save -->
  <section>
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <h2 id="save">Save with assertions</h2>
      <CodeBlock filename="shell" id="docs-save" code={SAVE_EXAMPLE} />
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Promotes a recording into <code>REPRO.md</code> with a title and assertions. Assertions are checked during replay.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Assertions -->
  <section>
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <h2 id="assertions">Assertion types</h2>
      <div class="assertion-list">
        {ASSERTION_TYPES.map(a => (
          <div class="assertion">
            <span class="assertion-type">{a.type}</span>
            <span class="assertion-desc">{a.desc}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CLI Reference -->
  <section>
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <h2 id="commands">CLI reference</h2>
      <div class="assertion-list">
        {CLI_COMMANDS.map(c => (
          <div class="assertion">
            <span class="assertion-type">{c.cmd}</span>
            <span class="assertion-desc">{c.desc}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- File structure -->
  <section>
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <h2 id="files">File structure</h2>
      <CodeBlock filename=".repro/" id="docs-file-structure" code={FILE_STRUCTURE} />
      <CodeBlock filename="REPRO.md" id="docs-repro-md" code={REPRO_MD_CONTENT} />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CI -->
  <section>
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <h2 id="ci">CI setup</h2>
      <CodeBlock filename=".github/workflows/repro.yml" lang="yaml" id="docs-ci" code={CI_WORKFLOW} />
      <div class="prose">
        <p>No API key needed. The replay proxy serves responses from the recorded trace. The agent binary (e.g. <code>claude</code>) must be available on the runner.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Base>
